    "taxonId": 169872,
    "summary": "Trailing perennial herb native to the Gulf Coast of eastern Mexico, from Tamaulipas to Yucatan. Wild plants are washed-out grey-green-purple, while the commercially grown 'Purpurea' cultivar has purple-violet leaves and stems. Its three-petalled flowers open only in the morning.",
